framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0021:
  description |
    Engine-owned live state must survive bucket continuation, semantic
    derive must not clobber fighter world, and TypeScript contract
    types must not be discarded.

problem P1:
  |
    v0.22.0-rc.5 battle btl_2788b1aba227a7ecd768b75270676423 executed
    38 reposition events and finished HP 109/109 with pairRelations
    still separate_area updatedTurn 0. ADR-0020 hops ran inside
    executeAction then vanished at bucket stop. BattleState is an
    open bag via as any and Record<string, any>, so the compiler
    cannot require that engine mutations appear on the continuation.

premise DRIVER_CHECKPOINT:
  |
    A bucket stop freezes BattleState. Only fields named on the
    engine continuation are live. The continuation must be the
    engine-owned live snapshot, not a v0.17 HP allow-list.

premise DRIVER_AUTHORITY:
  |
    worldState is server-owned mechanical fact. Fighter placement
    and the character.a/b pair are engine-owned after a hop.
    Semantic derive may update environment meaning; it must not
    restore spawn spacing.

premise DRIVER_TYPES:
  |
    Contract types must remain closed TypeScript. Escapes are
    forbidden on new code and on a path whose defect is under
    repair, except a non-contract hole that is individually
    audited and locked by a test.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Considered options are: append worldState to the continuation
    allow-list only; fast-forward reposition across the whole band
    as the diagnosis; or name the engine-owned live snapshot,
    close the BattleState type escape on this contract, and stop
    semantic clobber of fighter world. Allow-list-only leaves the
    next executeAction field to vanish. Time-skip does not explain
    updatedTurn 0. The live-snapshot plus closed types is the
    producing repair.

evidence E_BATTLE:
  |
    Production v0.22.0-rc.5 battle
    btl_2788b1aba227a7ecd768b75270676423: wait 34, reposition 38,
    requested basic_attack 37, world revision 0, pair separate_area
    updatedTurn 0. RCA
    docs/v0.22.0-rc.5-reposition-theater-rca.llmthink.dsl and
    docs/v0.22.0-rc.5-continuation-world-drop-root-rca.llmthink.dsl
    audited fatal=0.

evidence E_RETURN:
  |
    resolveTurn on bucket stop returns state: input.state.
    BattleTurnEngineContinuationSchema omitted worldState.
    materializeBattleStateAtBucketBoundary copied combatants, not
    world. Source: packages/shared/src/battle-engine.ts.

evidence E_TYPES:
  |
    BattleStateSchema ended `}) as any`. BattleState was a short
    explicit bag plus Record<string, any>. sceneBeat and perception
    frames were any. backend tsconfig set noImplicitAny false.
    Source: packages/shared/src/battle.ts and backend/tsconfig.json.

evidence E_DERIVE:
  |
    deriveBattleWorldTransitionFromSemanticState emits set_placement
    for character.a/b from semantic labels and set_pair_relation to
    near or separate_area, ignoring engine in-area ranks.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-06 the product owner instructed: forbid type escapes
    going forward; audit and test-lock only non-contract exceptions;
    do not retrofit every historical escape; new additions and found
    defects are mandatory; then implement this repair.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVER_CHECKPOINT, OPTIONS, E_RETURN, E_BATTLE:
  |
    Engine-owned live fields that must survive a bucket stop are
    combatants, finishers, pendingEffects, situation,
    defensiveInstrumentMultipliers, worldState, and
    latestWorldTransition. Continuation carries that snapshot.
    materialize and finalize restore it. resolveTurn must not return
    the pre-bucket BattleState after a world mutation.

decision D2 based_on DRIVER_AUTHORITY, E_DERIVE, E_BATTLE:
  |
    Semantic derive must not overwrite character.a/b placement or
    the fighter pair. Environment entities may still sync from
    semantic locations.

decision D3 based_on DRIVER_TYPES, E_TYPES, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    Type escapes are banned on new code and on a repaired defect
    path. Contract types cannot host an escape. Historical escapes
    elsewhere stay until found. Annotate BattleStateSchema as
    ZodType<BattleState>, not any. Name worldState,
    causalEngineContinuation, latestWorldTransition, and
    pendingEffects on BattleState so they are not any. TS7056
    still blocks z.infer of the full schema; remaining unnamed
    keys stay historically open until a defect names them. A
    colocated test must fail if the continuation is an open
    string index or those live fields become any.

decision D4 based_on OPTIONS, E_BATTLE:
  |
    Do not replace one-step reposition with a time-skip as this
    repair. Adjacent spawn plus a landed hop is enough for
    same_area strikes on a later beat. Compress-to-band remains a
    later product ADR if long maps still walk.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    ADR-0021 is Accepted at this owner-approved revision.
    Implementation of D1 through D3 is authorized. ADR-0020 remains
    Accepted; this record amends the checkpoint and type contract,
    not the reposition kind or substitution reasons.
